        <div class="presentation-case-study">
            <div class="case-study-top-grid">
                <div class="case-study-scenario-card">
                    <div class="scenario-badge">MODULE 08 - CASE STUDY 2: EMERGENCY UNBLINDING</div>
                    <div class="scenario-body-text">A participant develops severe toxicity, and the treating physician believes knowledge of treatment assignment is needed for medical care. The site unblinds without recording the reason.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="case-study-discussion-card">
                    <div class="discussion-heading">REGULATORY ASSESSMENT & DISCUSSION</div>
                    <ul class="discussion-list">
                        <li class="discussion-item"><span class="disc-marker">▸</span><span>Emergency unblinding may be appropriate when medically necessary.</span></li><li class="discussion-item"><span class="disc-marker">▸</span><span>The process and reason must be documented.</span></li><li class="discussion-item"><span class="disc-marker">▸</span><span>Notify the sponsor promptly.</span></li><li class="discussion-item"><span class="disc-marker">▸</span><span>Assess impact on participant safety and trial analysis.</span></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="case-study-takeaway-card"><strong>KEY REGULATORY TAKEAWAY:</strong> Emergency unblinding is controlled, justified and traceable.</div>
        </div>
        
        </div>
        
    <div class="slide-presentation-footer">
