            <div class="case-study-top-grid">
                <div class="case-study-scenario-card">
                    <div class="scenario-badge">MODULE 08 - CASE STUDY 2: API TRACEABILITY FAILURE</div>
                    <div class="scenario-body-text">A formulation site cannot identify the exact API lot used in a clinical-trial batch.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="case-study-discussion-card">
                    <div class="discussion-heading">REGULATORY ASSESSMENT & DISCUSSION</div>
                    <ul class="discussion-list">
                        <li class="discussion-item"><span class="disc-marker">▸</span><span>The batch may be unsuitable for release pending investigation.</span></li><li class="discussion-item"><span class="disc-marker">▸</span><span>Review batch records and supplier qualification.</span></li><li class="discussion-item"><span class="disc-marker">▸</span><span>Assess product identity, quality and participant impact.</span></li><li class="discussion-item"><span class="disc-marker">▸</span><span>Implement lot-level traceability.</span></li>
                    </ul>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="case-study-takeaway-card"><strong>KEY REGULATORY TAKEAWAY:</strong> API traceability is fundamental to product quality and trial accountability.</div>
        </div>
        
        </div>
        
