    </div>
    
        <div class="slide-content-area">
            
        <div class="presentation-lecture-slide">
            <div class="lecture-lead-text">Relaxation, abbreviation, omission or deferment may be considered case by case for:</div>
            <ul class="lecture-items-list">
        <li class="lecture-list-item icon-arrow">
            <span class="item-symbol">▸</span>
            <span class="item-content">Life-threatening diseases.</span>
        </li>
        
        <li class="lecture-list-item icon-arrow">
            <span class="item-symbol">▸</span>
            <span class="item-content">Serious diseases.</span>
        </li>
        
        <li class="lecture-list-item icon-arrow">
            <span class="item-symbol">▸</span>
            <span class="item-content">Rare diseases.</span>
        </li>
        
        <li class="lecture-list-item icon-arrow">
            <span class="item-symbol">▸</span>
            <span class="item-content">Unmet medical need.</span>
        </li>
        
        <li class="lecture-list-item icon-arrow">
            <span class="item-symbol">▸</span>
            <span class="item-content">Diseases of special relevance to India.</span>
        </li>
        
        <li class="lecture-list-item icon-arrow">
            <span class="item-symbol">▸</span>
            <span class="item-content">Disaster or defence-related needs.</span>
        </li>
        
        <li class="lecture-list-item icon-arrow">
            <span class="item-symbol">▸</span>
            <span class="item-content">Certain emergency public-health situations.</span>
        </li>
        
        <li class="lecture-list-item icon-arrow">
            <span class="item-symbol">▸</span>
            <span class="item-content">Relaxation does not mean that evidence is unnecessary.</span>
        </li>
        </ul>
            
